      {
        "question_text": "Write an algebraic expression for each description.\n(a) The product of $7$ and $k$.\n(b) One third of $h$.\n(c) $r$ subtracted from $15$.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Product means multiply.\n$7\\times k=7k$\n(b) One third means divide by $3$.\n$h\\div3=\\frac{h}{3}$\n(c) Start with $15$ and subtract $r$. The expression is $15-r$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Write an algebraic expression for each description.\n(a) Triple $u$, then add $5$.\n(b) Add $5$ to $u$, then triple the result.\n(c) The square of the sum of $v$ and $2$.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Triple $u$ gives $3u$, then add $5$. The expression is $3u+5$.\n(b) First form the sum $u+5$. Triple the **whole sum**, so use brackets. The expression is $3(u+5)$.\n(c) First form $v+2$, then square the whole sum. The expression is $(v+2)^2$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) Write $12-3p$ in words.\n(b) A worker is paid $w$ dollars per hour. The hourly rate rises by $5$ dollars. The worker then works $6$ hours. Write an expression for the pay.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $3p$ means triple $p$. Subtract that from $12$.\nIn words: triple $p$ subtracted from $12$.\n(b) The new hourly rate is $w+5$ dollars. Multiply the whole rate by $6$.\nThe pay is $6(w+5)$ dollars."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Write an algebraic expression for each description.\n(a) The sum of $9$ and $b$.\n(b) $4$ less than $t$.\n(c) $5$ more than half of $m$.\n(d) $8$ less than the product of $5$ and $z$.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Sum means add. The expression is $9+b$.\n(b) Start with $t$ and subtract $4$. The expression is $t-4$.\n(c) Half of $m$ is $\\frac{m}{2}$, then add $5$. The expression is $\\frac{m}{2}+5$.\n(d) The product is $5z$, then subtract $8$. The expression is $5z-8$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Write an algebraic expression for each description.\n(a) $6$ is subtracted from $j$, then the result is multiplied by $7$.\n(b) $q$ is subtracted from $18$, then the result is multiplied by $4$.",
        "solution_text": "(a) First form $j-6$. Multiply the **whole difference** by $7$, so use brackets. The expression is $7(j-6)$.\n(b) Start with $18$ and subtract $q$. Multiply the **whole difference** by $4$. The expression is $4(18-q)$."
      }
    ],
